# MERGE-PARENT-MODEL-SOURCE, a sub occurrence held by a callable formal: `recv(b1\bump)` hands f the occurrence
# the path selects when the root is walked -- b1's own, under C, the copy of the unit; natively the unit's own
# (COPIED-CALLABLE-ACTUAL, steps/defects.md) -- and `f()` admits the free input a3 (recv's own, formed from the root's)
# to the requirement read in the space of the occurrence f holds, not recv's.  The write lands in the root's a3 (3).
# recv keeps its native word in the walked twin (a callable formal).  HEAD refused it walked.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 2
end: Wide
sub: bump ()
    a3\x: a3\x + 1
end: bump
Box:
    int: v 0
    fn: bump
end: Box
fn: recv (bump: f) int
    f()
    return: 0
end: recv
b1: merge: Box
a3: merge: Wide
int: r recv(b1\bump)
int: ok 7
if: a3\x != 3 || a3\pad != 9
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
